  "summary": "An engine-driven generator uses a reciprocating engine as the prime mover to turn a generator. In this spark-ignition gas engine, fuel–air mixture burns in each cylinder and pushes the pistons down; the crankshaft turns the flywheel and the generator rotor, which induces AC voltage in the stator. The governor holds the speed constant so the frequency stays at 50 or 60 Hz.",
